  "id": "voluntary-admission",
  "term": "voluntary admission",
  "definition": "In this historical context, voluntary admission meant entry to an asylum at the request of the patient’s family rather than by public authority order. It required supporting documents, including a request for admission, a recent medical certificate on the person’s mental state and need for asylum care, and proof of identity, with official oversight to guard against improper confinement.",
